        "json": {
          "text": "```cpp\nvoid showVotePercentages()\n{\n    // Print a header to indicate the start of vote percentages display\n    cout << \"===== VOTE PERCENTAGES =====\" << endl;\n\n    // Loop through all candidates to calculate and display their vote percentages\n    for (int i = 0; i < totalCandidates; i++)\n    {\n        // Initialize percentage variable for the current candidate\n        double percentage = 0;\n\n        // Check to avoid division by zero if there are no voters\n        if (totalVoters > 0)\n        {\n            // Calculate the percentage of total votes the current candidate received\n            percentage = (double)voteCounts[i] / totalVoters * 100;\n        }\n\n        // Output the candidate's party name and their corresponding vote percentage\n        cout << partyNames[i] << \" : \" << percentage << \"%\" << endl;\n    }\n}\n```"
        },
        "pairedItem": {
          "item": 0
        }
      },
      {
        "json": {
          "text": "This code defines a function called `showVotePercentages()` that prints the voting results for different parties. It first shows a heading \"===== VOTE PERCENTAGES =====\". Then, for each candidate, it calculates the percentage of total votes they received by dividing their votes by the total number of voters, only if there is at least one voter. Finally, it prints each party's name followed by their vote percentage. This helps to quickly see how much support each candidate got in terms of percentage."
        },
